===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|goh|stunta}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*stundō||point in time, hour}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|stond||time}}, {{cog|en|stound||hour, while}}, {{cog|da|stund||while}}, {{cog|no|stund||while}}, {{cog|se|stund||while}}. More at {{l|en|stound}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈʃtʊndə/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-Stunde.ogg|audio (Germany)|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-at-Stunde.ogg|audio (Austria)|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f||Stunden|Stündchen|dim2=Stündlein}}

# [[hour]] {{gloss|unit of time constisting of 60 minutes}}
#: {{ux|de|Der Film dauert drei '''Stunden'''.|The movie lasts three '''hours.'''}}
# {{lb|de|dated}} [[hour]]; [[stound]]; [[moment]] {{gloss|point in time}}
#: {{ux|de|Bitte für uns Sünder, jetzt und in der '''Stunde''' unsres Todes.|Pray for us sinners, now and at the '''hour''' of our death.}}
# [[lesson]]; [[class]] {{gloss|unit of instruction, typically between 45 and 90 minutes}}
#: {{ux|de|Ich muss jetzt zur Klavier'''stunde.'''|I need to go to piano '''class''' right now.}}

